#
# File: filters.lut
#
# Database of available GMOS filters.
#
# This file contains a list of all the filters known to GMOS,
# whether fitted or not. Each time a new filter is purchased
# it should be assigned a barcode and added to this list.
#
# Surface curvature focus offsets come from measurements by Jeremy
# Allington-Smith, Isobel Hook and Stephanie Juneau on 7 July 2000.
# Effective wavelengths supplied by Isobel Hook on 24 January 2001.
# Names suggested by Inger Jorgensen on 31 January 2001.
# 
# GMOS-N filter table updated with information sent by
# Kathy Roth. Commented out all GMOS-N filters.
# New GMOS-N filters added: OIII, OIIIC, SII, HeII and HeIIC
# R. Carrasco - 2009 June 08
#
# GMOS-S filter lut re-organized.  Removed old GMOS-S focus
# offsets from Acceptance Test. Also removed all commented empty
# slots from filter cells. Only one slot is available for a future
# filter in filter wheel #2. 
# R. Carrasco - 2009jun08
#
#                                 surface curvature
# name            barcodeId       focusOffset (microns)   effWavelength (nm)
# GMOS South Empty filter cells - to be filled and barcodes reused
# Bar code 20000047 for emty_11 does not exist. The correct bar code is
# 20000036 (from flt.lut). R. Carrasco - 2009jun08
